<figure class="cache-figure" data-age-budget>
 <p class="figure-title">The answer starts ageing before it reaches Redis</p>
 <div class="cache-controls"><label>Loading delay <input type="range" min="0" max="12" value="4" data-delay aria-label="Loading delay"/><output data-delay-value>4 s</output></label><label>Redis TTL <input type="range" min="1" max="12" value="6" data-ttl aria-label="Freshness budget TTL"/><output data-ttl-value>6 s</output></label></div>
 <p class="figure-note">From the source observation → loading → saved copy → expiry</p>
 <div class="age-track" aria-hidden="true"><i data-loading></i><i data-cached></i></div>
 <div class="age-legend"><span>Loading: <b data-load-label>4 s</b></span><span>In Redis: <b data-cache-label>6 s</b></span></div>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>Bar lengths share a fixed 24-second scale. A single current source observation, bounded loading, no other copies, and no expiry renewal. The bound is approached just before expiry; requests need not occur at that exact age. Replica staleness and additional cache layers require their own budget.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-age-budget]').forEach(root=>{
 const delay=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-delay]')!,ttl=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-ttl]')!;
 const set=(n:string,v:string)=>{root.querySelector(`[data-${n}]`)!.textContent=v;};
 const render=()=>{const d=+delay.value,t=+ttl.value;set('delay-value',`${d} s`);set('ttl-value',`${t} s`);set('load-label',`${d} s`);set('cache-label',`${t} s`);root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-loading]')!.style.width=`${d/24*100}%`;root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-cached]')!.style.width=`${t/24*100}%`;set('explanation',`${d} seconds loading + ${t} seconds in Redis = ${d+t} seconds from source observation to expiry. ${d?'The TTL accounts for only the second part.':'With immediate loading, the TTL accounts for the whole interval.'}`);};delay.oninput=render;ttl.oninput=render;render();
});
</script>
